title: Radek in the Lobby
subtitle: Moscow's man has a proposal for every delegation.
view-if: congress_leipzig = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and e23_lz_radek_used = 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.e23_lz_radek_used = 1;
RG.congress.tally();
Q.e23_lz_radek_name = (typeof Q.comintern_rep === 'string' && Q.comintern_rep) ? Q.comintern_rep : 'Karl Radek';
Q.e23_lz_with_moscow = (Q.moscow_backs == Q.congress_backing) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_lz_has_rival = Q.congress_rival ? 1 : 0;
Q.sys_outcome = 0;
!}
frequency: 150
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= Radek in the Lobby

[+ e23_lz_radek_name +] has spent the congress in the lobby with a cigarette and a different joke for every delegation. In the evening he sends for our whips. The Executive wants a strong Zentrale and an unbroken party, he says, and does not much mind who leads it as long as both sides are inside. [? if e23_lz_with_moscow = 1 : He would be glad to say from the platform that Moscow is with our motion. ?][? if e23_lz_with_moscow = 0 : The Executive's sympathies, he admits, lie with the [+ moscow_backs_name +]. ?]

- @compromise: Take his compromise with the [+ congress_rival_name +].
- @speak: Ask him to speak.
- @decline: Tell him the German party will settle this itself.

@compromise
subtitle: Their delegates vote with us, and they share the Zentrale if we win.
view-if: e23_lz_has_rival = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_lz_deal_name = Q.congress_rival_name;
RG.congress.deal(Q.congress_rival);
RG.ecci('radek', 8);
Q.independence -= 3;
!}

Two hours in a back room, a bottle of Saxon brandy and a list of names. The [+ e23_lz_deal_name +] withdraw their motion.

@speak
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] If Moscow is with us he can move the hall. If it is not, he will say so.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('moscow_orders', 5);
if (Q.e23_lz_with_moscow == 1) {
    RG.congress.sway(0.08);
    Q.sys_outcome = 1;
} else {
    RG.congress.swayTo(Q.moscow_backs, 0.05);
    Q.sys_outcome = 2;
}
Q.independence -= 3;
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
!}

[? if sys_outcome = 1 : Radek speaks for forty minutes in better German than most of the delegates, and [+ congress_last_moved +] of them come over to us. ?][? if sys_outcome = 2 : Radek speaks for the Executive, which means for the [+ moscow_backs_name +], and [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates go over to them. ?]

@decline
subtitle: The delegates who dislike being told what to do will like it. Radek will not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 4;
RG.ecci('radek', -8);
RG.congress.sway(0.02);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

We thank the Executive's representative for his advice. Radek's report to Zinoviev that night runs to two pages.
